Package: banditlab
Title: Multi-Armed Bandit Experimentation and Policy Comparison
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Mubanga", "Nsofu", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "ProDigest@Protonmail.com")
Description: A framework for simulating, comparing and extending multi-armed
    bandit algorithms. Provides stochastic reward environments, classical
    policies (random, greedy, epsilon-greedy, explore-then-commit, upper
    confidence bound, Thompson sampling), a replicated experiment engine with
    reproducible per-replicate random number streams, mathematically explicit
    pseudo-regret metrics, tidy result objects and accessible default plots.
    Custom policies can be added through a small documented S3 interface
    without modifying the package. Methods follow Lattimore and Szepesvari
    (2020, ISBN:9781108486828) and Sutton and Barto (2018, ISBN:9780262039246).
License: MIT + file LICENSE
